/H /N
/Rect [96.408 473.418 513.399 742.404]
/Subtype /Widget
/T (tooltip zref@1)
/TU (Diagram illustrating an architecture, with seven layers labelled from A to G. Each layer represents a specific function: Layer A: Physical world, involving things, assets, and actuators. Layer B: Data acquisition, focussed on accessing, assessing, converting, and aggregating signals. Layer C: Data management, encompassing governance, preparation, and quality control. Layer D: Data protection, involving archiving, backups, snapshots, replication, availability, and disaster recovery. Layer E: Data processing, covering storage systems, assets, and preparation of data for processing. Layer F: Data analytics, including descriptive, predictive, and prescriptive analytics. Layer G: Data visualisation and user interface, covering graphical interfaces and interactions between humans and machines. Adjacent to the layers are additional vertical considerations: configuring security policies and addressing vulnerabilities.)
/Type /Annot
>>
